# The public repo holds ONLY the finished website.
#
# Huck's rule (2026-07-29): GitHub should contain the finished project code and
# nothing else — no build pipeline, no source data, no working notes, no docs.
# Everything listed below stays on the local machine only.
#
# What IS published, deliberately:
#   site/                the finished map — this is the product
#   .github/workflows/   the Pages deploy; without it nothing goes live
#   .gitignore           this file
#
# WARNING: everything below now exists ONLY on this Mac and is not backed up
# anywhere. Losing the machine loses the build pipeline and the pin database.

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- build pipeline & source data (local only) ---
scripts/
data/
publish.sh

# --- project docs & working notes (local only) ---
notes/
CLAUDE.md
HOW-TO.md
todo.md
done.md
.claude/
